  "G66ID52Y": {
    "quotes": [
      {
        "role": "system",
        "value": "News summarization",
        "text": "Google is beginning to replace news headlines in its search results with ones that are AI-generated",
        "start": 338,
        "end": 437
      },
      {
        "role": "harm",
        "value": "Distorted source representation",
        "text": "We’ve found multiple examples where Google replaced headlines we wrote with ones we did not, sometimes changing their meaning in the process.\nFor example, Google reduced our headline “I used the ‘cheat on everything’ AI tool and it didn’t help me cheat on anything” to just five words: “‘Cheat on everything’ AI tool.” It almost sounds like we’re endorsing a product we do not recommend at all.",
        "start": 581,
        "end": 975
      },
      {
        "role": "factor",
        "value": "Lack of audience disclosure",
        "text": "without any indication that Google replaced the words we chose.",
